  "lean": {
    "statement": "(n : ℕ) (h : (Fin n → Bool) → ℝ) :\n    let μ : Measure (Fin n → Bool) :=\n      (Fintype.card (Fin n → Bool) : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ • Measure.count\n    let D := fun ε : Fin n → Bool =>\n      ∑ j : Fin n, (h ε - h (Function.update ε j (!ε j))) ^ 2\n    IsProbabilityMeasure μ ∧\n      Integrable (fun ε => (h ε) ^ 2) μ ∧\n      Integrable (fun ε => (h ε) ^ 2 * Real.log ((h ε) ^ 2)) μ ∧\n      Integrable D μ ∧\n      ((∫ ε, (h ε) ^ 2 * Real.log ((h ε) ^ 2) ∂μ) -\n        (∫ ε, (h ε) ^ 2 ∂μ) * Real.log (∫ ε, (h ε) ^ 2 ∂μ) ≤\n      (1 / 2 : ℝ) * ∫ ε, D ε ∂μ)",
    "statement_sha256": "c468f7ca804319897f172655fa3fcde108c1e66df67759f254e89d35aca5582b",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "Fin n is the finite type of indices less than n; Bool has two values. The carrier is all functions Fin n -> Bool with its canonical finite measurable structure, including n=0.",
      "Measure.count is counting measure. Fintype.card is the actual carrier cardinal. Scalar multiplication by its inverse in ENNReal gives literal normalized counting measure. IsProbabilityMeasure asserts total mass one.",
      "Function.update replaces only the indicated coordinate by Bool.not of its old value. D is the unnormalized sum of full-flip difference squares over all coordinates. No half factor is hidden in D.",
      "Integrable is true Bochner integrability under the displayed measure; every one is an output. Real.log0=0, so zero-square entropy contributions are zero. The left expression is homogeneous function entropy of h squared, with its actual mean-square normalization.",
      "h is an arbitrary signed real function; n=0, zeros and all constants remain admitted. There are no supplied entropy, smoothness, law, domain, independence or inequality certificates."
    ]
  },
